## 📄 1. Analytics Page

**Layunin:** Bigyan ng data-driven insights ang streamer – viewers, followers, subscribers, at engagement.

### Main Dashboard
- [ ] **Live metrics** – current viewers, follower count (real-time)
- [ ] **Stream health** – bitrate, fps drops, dropped frames (kung connected sa OBS)
- [ ] **Revenue estimate** – ads, bits, subs (daily/weekly/monthly)
- [ ] **Top performing clips** – views, likes, creation date

### Charts & Graphs (filterable by date range)
- [ ] **Follower growth** – line graph (7d, 30d, all time)
- [ ] **Subscriber points** (cumulative subs + resubs)
- [ ] **Chat activity heatmap** – kung kailan active ang chat
- [ ] **Game/category performance** – aling laro ang pinakamataas ang viewers

### Export & Sharing
- [ ] I‑download bilang PNG/CSV
- [ ] I‑share ng naka‑embed na image (for social media)

> **Gagamiting services:** `twitch-api.service` (get streams, followers, subscriptions), `history.service` (watch history), `clips.service`

---

## 📄 2. Moderation Page

**Layunin:** I‑manage ang chat, bans, timeouts, at i‑filter ang spam/hate speech.

### Chat Moderation Tools
- [ ] **Chat feed** – live view ng channel chat (gamit ang `twitch-chat.service`)
- [ ] **Quick actions** – timeout (1m,5m,10m,30m), ban, unban
- [ ] **User info panel** – badges, follower since, sub tier, previous warnings
- [ ] **Message filter** – awtomatikong i‑hide o i‑flag ang mga message na may banned words (gamit `chatFilters` sa settings)

### Automation Rules
- [ ] **Auto‑timeout** – kapag may link, caps >70%, spam na emoji
- [ ] **Blocked words list** – galing sa `settingsService.chatFilters`
- [ ] **Allow list** (trusted users exempted)

### Moderation Logs
- [ ] Talaan ng lahat ng bans/timeouts (kailan, sino, dahilan)
- [ ] **Undo** button (unban / remove timeout)

### Team Management
- [ ] Listahan ng moderators (galing `streamManagerService.getModerators`)
- [ ] Mag‑add / mag‑remove ng mod

> **Gagamiting services:** `twitch-chat.service` (send messages, bans/timeouts), `settingsService` (chatFilters), `stream-manager.service` (moderators, ban, timeout)

---

## 📄 3. Creator Dashboard

**Layunin:** Isang summary page ng lahat ng mahahalagang impormasyon at actions para sa streamer.

### Stream Info (editable)
- [ ] **Stream title** – inline edit (gamit `streamManagerService.updateStreamInfo`)
- [ ] **Game/category** – searchable dropdown (gamit `gamesService.searchCategories`)
- [ ] **Tags** – multi‑select
- [ ] **Language** – dropdown

### Recent Activity Feed (gamit `notificationStore`)
- [ ] Latest 10 events: follows, subs, raids, hype train (naka‑group)
- [ ] Click event → mag‑show ng modal o mag‑jump sa chat/analytics

### Quick Actions
- [ ] **Start / stop stream** (kung naka‑integrate sa OBS)
- [ ] **Run commercial** (30s, 60s) – `streamManagerService.runCommercial`
- [ ] **Create clip** (last 30s) – `streamManagerService.createClip`
- [ ] **Send shoutout** sa isang channel – `streamManagerService.sendShoutout`
- [ ] **Start raid** – `streamManagerService.startRaid`

### Alerts & Reminders
- [ ] **Go‑live notification** preview (test)
- [ ] **Reminder** para mag‑update ng title / tags kung more than 2 hours na ang stream
- [ ] **Ad schedule** – countdown hanggang next ad break

### Stream Goals (gamit `streamManagerService` goals)
- [ ] Mag‑set ng goal: followers, subs, bits (may progress bar)
- [ ] I‑edit / i‑delete ang goal
- [ ] I‑display sa overlay (kung naka‑browser source)

> **Gagamiting services:** `stream-manager.service`, `gamesService`, `notificationStore`, `obsWebSocketService` (kung gusto mong Start/Stop stream)

---

## 📄 4. Stream Settings (o i‑merge na lang sa Creator Dashboard?)

**Layunin:** Ayusin ang technical settings para sa stream. Pwede mo itong gawing tab sa loob ng Creator Dashboard.

- [ ] **Stream title, category, tags, language** (duplicate sa Creator Dashboard – kaya pwedeng i‑remove)
- [ ] **Stream key** (ipapakita kasama ng copy button) – `streamManagerService.getStreamKey`
- [ ] **Ingest server** selection (listahan mula `twitchApiService.getIngestServers`)
- [ ] **Latency mode** (normal / low latency)
- [ ] **VOD settings** – i‑auto‑publish o i‑disable ang VOD
- [ ] **ADS settings** – pre‑roll, mid‑roll
- [ ] **Muted sections** (Twitch Soundtrack) – i‑toggle
- [ ] **Stream markers** (create marker)

> **Kung gugustuhin mong tanggalin ang Stream Settings page:**  
> Ilipat mo na lang ang **Stream Key**, **Ingest server**, at **VOD settings** sa Creator Dashboard bilang expandable section o modal. Hindi naman araw‑araw ginagalaw ang mga ito.

---

## 📄 5. Settings Page (App‑wide preferences)

**Layunin:** I‑customize ang gawi ng mismong application.

### General
- [ ] **Theme** (light/dark/system) – `themesService`
- [ ] **Language** (kung multi‑lingual)
- [ ] **Auto‑play** video when opening player – `settingsService.autoPlay`

### Notifications
- [ ] **Desktop notifications** – On/Off (gamit `notificationService`)
- [ ] **Anong events ang mag‑notify** – follow, sub, raid, hype train, stream online (checkbox)
- [ ] **Test notification** button

### Chat & Moderation
- [ ] **Blocked words list** (add/remove) – `settingsService.addChatFilter`
- [ ] **Automod level** (none, basic, aggressive)
- [ ] **Chat delay** (seconds)

### Keyboard Shortcuts
- [ ] Play/Pause, Next/Previous channel, Volume Up/Down, Mute, Fullscreen – gamit `shortcutService`
- [ ] I‑customize ang key combinations

### OBS WebSocket
- [ ] **Auto‑connect** checkbox
- [ ] **Host / Port** (default localhost:4455)
- [ ] **Password** (naka‑store sa `obs-websocket.service`)
- [ ] **Test connection** button

### Accounts
- [ ] **Mag‑add ng multiple Twitch accounts** (gamit `twitchAuthService.loginNewAccount`)
- [ ] **Switch account** – walang logout, direct switch
- [ ] **Remove account**
- [ ] **Export / Import** settings & accounts (JSON)

### Data & Storage
- [ ] **Clear watch history** – `historyService.clearHistory`
- [ ] **Clear notification cache** – `notificationStore.clearAll`
- [ ] **Reset all settings** – `settingsService.reset`

### Automation Defaults (galing `automationService`)
- [ ] **Auto‑raid** target channel
- [ ] **Auto‑clip** on stream offline
- [ ] **Auto‑message** text (placeholder: `Thanks for the follow/sub! 🎉`)
- [ ] I‑enable/disable kada automation

### About / Updates
- [ ] **Version number** (mula `package.json`)
- [ ] **Check for updates** (gamit `electron-updater`)
- [ ] **Open log folder** – `logger`

---

## ✅ Recap: Anong page ang dapat mong unahin?

| Page | Priority | Dahil |
|------|----------|-------|
| **Creator Dashboard** | 🔴 High | Dito mo makikita at mae-edit ang stream info, plus quick actions – ito ang puso ng app para sa streamer |
| **Moderation** | 🟠 High | Kailangan para sa live chat management, lalo na kung maraming viewers |
| **Analytics** | 🟡 Medium | Hindi kailangan sa unang release pero maganda para sa insights |
| **Settings** | 🟡 Medium | Kailangan para i‑customize ang app, pero pwedeng gawin sa huli |
| **Stream Settings** | ⚪ Low (merge) | I‑merge mo na lang sa Creator Dashboard para iwas duplication |

---

## 🧠 Mga karagdagang ideya (kung gusto mong lumampas)

- **Scheduled events** – mag‑schedule ng stream title/game change, o commercial break
- **Chat bot commands** – `!so`, `!clip`, `!lurk`, `!uptime` – gamit ang `twitch-chat.service` + `automationService`
- **Stream overlay preview** – i‑preview ang browser source (goals, recent events)
- **Twitch Polls & Predictions** – gumamit ng `predictionsService` para gumawa/manage ng polls mula sa app

Kung gusto mo, pwedeng gawan kita ng **actual component structure** (React) para sa isa sa mga page na ito – halimbawa, ang **Creator Dashboard**. Sabihin mo lang!











































## 1️⃣ **Layout & Responsiveness**

| # | Task | Priority | Description |
|---|------|----------|-------------|
| 1.1 | Replace hardcoded grid with dynamic CSS Grid using Tailwind’s `grid-cols-` and `minmax` | High | Current grid uses fixed column widths (`[1.5fr_1fr_1fr_1fr]`). On smaller screens it may overflow. Use `grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4` with `gap-4` and let cards stretch. |
| 1.2 | Add a resize observer to adjust card heights | Medium | Cards like `ChatCard` and `CustomAutomationsCard` have different heights; ensure they align nicely. Use `h-full` and `flex-col`. |
| 1.3 | Improve mobile layout (sidebar open state) | Low | The page currently assumes desktop; add `overflow-x-auto` on the grid container and consider a stacked layout on screens < 768px. |

---

## 2️⃣ **Core Functionality Improvements**

### 🎬 **MainVideoCard**

| # | Task | Priority | Description |
